  "theorem_name": "PolylogarithmicSquarefreePrimeShellAsymptoticAndSparseDenominatorNoGo",
  "declared_proposition": "For every odd squarefree q and nonnegative residue masses with mean mu and maximum relative discrepancy epsilon, the reduced rational shell satisfies T_q(N)=mu^2 c_q(N)+R_q(N), with |R_q(N)|<=mu^2(2 phi(q)^2 epsilon+phi(q)^3 epsilon^2). Siegel-Walfisz therefore gives, for log-prime weights, uniformly for q<=(log X)^B and every N, T_(q,X)(N)=mu^2 c_q(N)+o_B(mu^2). For prime l the correction also obeys the exact Parseval identity. Without any q-X-N coupling, actual primes with l>2X+1 give a sparse cutoff family whose relative shell correction is l(l-2).",
  "mathematical_argument": "For a unit a and squarefree q, c_q(a)=Mobius(q). Writing the residue Fourier sum as mu*Mobius(q)+D_a gives |D_a|<=phi(q)epsilon mu; squaring and summing over phi(q) unit frequencies proves the bound. Siegel-Walfisz makes epsilon=O_B(q exp(-c_B sqrt(log X))), so the bound is o_B(mu^2) throughout the polylogarithmic squarefree range. Squarefree Ramanujan sums never vanish. Fourier Parseval gives sum_n|R_l(n)|^2=l sum_(a!=0)|S(a/l)^2-mu^2|^2. Finally, if l>2X+1 and N=l+2X+1, no pair p_1,p_2<=X reaches the target residue; the TICKET-232 identity gives T=-W^2 and the exact divergent ratio.",
