    "proof": "For a unit a and squarefree q, c_q(a)=Mobius(q). Writing the residue Fourier sum as mu*Mobius(q)+D_a gives |D_a|<=phi(q)epsilon mu; squaring and summing over phi(q) unit frequencies proves the bound. Siegel-Walfisz makes epsilon=O_B(q exp(-c_B sqrt(log X))), so the bound is o_B(mu^2) throughout the polylogarithmic squarefree range. Squarefree Ramanujan sums never vanish. Fourier Parseval gives sum_n|R_l(n)|^2=l sum_(a!=0)|S(a/l)^2-mu^2|^2. Finally, if l>2X+1 and N=l+2X+1, no pair p_1,p_2<=X reaches the target residue; the TICKET-232 identity gives T=-W^2 and the exact divergent ratio.",
